mevr 1.3.6 (release date: 2026-11-09)
=========================================

Changes:

* fsmev() with censor = TRUE now always returns the left-censoring quantile
  opt_quant and threshold opt_thresh (NA if the Weibull tail is rejected),
  and print() shows them.
* fsmev() with censor = TRUE and sd = TRUE: the bootstrap now refits the
  censored estimator at the left-censoring quantile found by the Weibull tail
  test. Before, it refitted the uncensored estimator, so std and varcov (and
  delta-method confidence intervals) did not belong to the censored c and w.
* Bootstrap confidence intervals of return levels (return.levels.mev() and
  plot() with ci = TRUE, method "boot") of fsmev() fits with censor = TRUE
  now refit the censored estimator at the left-censoring quantile.
* plot() works for fsmev() fits of a numeric vector. As there are no yearly
  maxima, the ordinary events are shown with the return period of the yearly
  maximum, 1 / (1 - F^n). The probability plot now has correct axis labels.
* print() and plot() show the estimator actually used for c and w: with
  censor = TRUE this is the least squares fit of the Weibull tail test.
* print() of fmev() fits with censor = TRUE shows the Weibull tail test, the
  left-censoring quantile and threshold for each year (the table was not
  printed before).


mevr 1.3.5 (release date: 2026-11-06)
=========================================

Changes:

* Dynamic censoring (censor = TRUE in fsmev() and fmev()) and
  weibull_tail_test() are much faster (about 100x for a full threshold scan):
  data preparation and synthetic samples are computed once for all censoring
  quantiles, and the order statistics of the synthetic samples are drawn
  directly from their Beta distribution instead of sorting R full samples.
* Bug fix in weibull_tail_test(): the R synthetic samples were all identical
  (recycled random numbers), so the test effectively used a single sample and
  its outcome depended strongly on the random seed. The selected censoring
  quantile can therefore differ from earlier versions.
* fmev() with censor = TRUE no longer warns "fitting uncensored SMEV" when
  warn = FALSE.
* plot() no longer fails for fmev() fits with censor = TRUE in which the
  Weibull tail of some years was rejected.
* The argument warn of censored_weibull_fit() now defaults to TRUE, as
  documented.


mevr 1.3.4 (release date: 2026-10-16)
=========================================

Changes:

* Added a delta-method for the calculation of confidence intervals of the SMEV.


mevr 1.3.3 (release date: 2026-10-13)
=========================================

Changes:

* Added some edge case tests to increase overall coverage.


mevr 1.3.2 (release date: 2026-10-12)
=========================================

Changes:

* Force data.table > 1.18.0 to ensure proper handling of NA values in large datasets


mevr 1.3.1 (release date: 2026-10-10)
=========================================

Changes:

* The data argument in fsmev now also accepts a vector.
* The set of independent storm events identified via event_separation now remains invariant across durations.


mevr 1.3.0 (release date: 2026-10-08)
=========================================

Changes:

* New argument left_cens in fsmev() and fmev(). With left_cens = 0.9, c and w come from the top 10 % of events while n still counts all of them.
* Ordinary_events() no longer drops rows; missing values are handled inside the rolling sum.
* Bootstrap confidence intervals now refit with the object's own method, threshold and left_cens; before, they always refitted with default PWM.


mevr 1.2.3 (release date: 2025-03-27)
=========================================

Changes:

* Included some tests for new functions for storm separation and ordinary events definition.


mevr 1.2.2 (release date: 2024-09-18)
=========================================

Changes:

* Two functions added for storm separation and definition of ordinary events.
* Functions fmsev, fmev and ftmev can now be used for sub-daily rainfall durations.


mevr 1.1.2 (release date: 2024-08-06)
=========================================

Changes:

* The Weibull tail test now returns the result to the fsmev function.
* Some tests were added.


mevr 1.1.1 (release date: 2024-06-21)
=========================================

Changes:

* A Weibull tail test based on left-censoring the input data can be performed
prior to fitting a SMEV. This can drastly improve fitting results.
* Some internal code improvements.


mevr 1.0.1 (release date: 2024-06-19)
=========================================

Changes:

* NA values are always removed. Functions fsmev, fmev and ftmev throw warnings
if the data contains any NA values.
* Some internal code improvements.
* Added more tests.


mevr 1.0.0 (release date: 2024-06-15)
=========================================

* First release, submitted to CRAN.
